R-2&#x0002f;neu, HLA-A2 peptide, p369&#x02013;377, results in short-lived peptide-specific immunity</article-title><source>Clin Cancer Res</source><year>2002</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1014</fpage><lpage>1018</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Clin Cancer Res||8|1014||bib17|'--></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Knutson</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Schiffman</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Disis</surname><given-names>ML</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Immunization with a HER-2&#x0002f;neu helper peptide vaccine generates HER-2&#x0002f;neu CD8 T-cell immunity in cancer patients</article-title><source>J Clin Invest</source><year>2001</year><volume>107</volume><fpage>477</fpage><lpage>484</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Invest||107|477||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11181647</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kono</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Halapi</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hising</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Petersson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerdin</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Vanky</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiessling</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanisms of escape from CD8&#x0002b; T-cell clones specific for the HER-2&#x0002f;neu proto-oncogene expressed in ovarian carcinomas: related and unrelated to decreased MHC class I expression</article-title><source>Int J Cancer</source><year>1997</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>112</fpage><lpage>119</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Int J Cancer||70|112||bib19|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8985099</pub-id></citati